== Procedural grass and terrain-buffer reuse

Grass now swaps between six-segment strips (14 vertices, 12 triangles) and low-detail tapered quads (4 vertices, 2 triangles). A narrow top edge preserves both low triangles. Current camera-to-triangle bounds select geometry without rebuilding roots, while the fragment shader evaluates a shared nonlinear palette so low detail retains the same base-to-tip color. Dithered pixel coverage replaces sinking; grass roots and heights stay fixed while coverage retires. The landscape retains its independent eight-level sinking.

The JSON `quad_distance_m` setting selects the morph endpoint in metres, with morphing starting at half that distance; zero preserves the automatic minimum of 15 m and one quarter of the grass draw distance. CPU draw selection and both shader paths share the threshold independently of root density. Interactive wind follows wall time independently of orbital pause and speed, with whole-frame reuse disabled while wind is animated. Fixed captures retain their explicit wind phase for reproducibility. The native `GrassWindInputIntegration` test waits for the completed surface transition, presses T and the speed keys, verifies changing grass pixels at fixed orbital time, reloads a zero wind speed and requires identical RGB frames. Removing foliage proves that the frozen view contained grass. Resolved scenes, images and traces are retained under `benchmarks/wind/`; see `benchmarks/live-wind.md`.

The quad transition now preserves interior shading by interpolating lateral offset and normalizing by local blade width per fragment. A neutral-light regression reproduced a 13-level RGB difference before the fix. Candidate acceptance uses a stable slot rank with a smooth density-coverage ramp, so crossing a power-of-two batch boundary no longer replaces existing visible roots. Compute/fallback position parity and both transition regressions pass.

